<title>UK: Norweb cuts electricity tariffs by 5.75 pct.</title>
<headline>Norweb cuts electricity tariffs by 5.75 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Regional electricity company Norweb, part of United Utilities, said it was cutting its tariffs by 5.75 percent from today.</p>
<p>As a result, the average domestic customer of Norweb, based in northwestern England, will see electricity bills fall by 15 stg a year, the company said..</p>
<p>The price cut, which follows a reduction in the fuel levy tax from November, means that the average customer will be paying less for electricity in real terms than in 1991, Norweb said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
